Falsifies `generational_table::verification::a_cleared_table_resolves_no_name_it_held`.

The defect: `clear` empties each slot without bumping its generation. Emptying is what a reader
expects a clear to do, and every lookup on the cleared table still answers `None`, because every
slot is empty; only the next insert shows the difference.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_ne!(next, Some(probe), ...)`, whenever the name was live
before the clear and the next insert takes its slot: the slot mints the cleared entry's name
again, so a name the caller still holds reaches the new occupant.
